  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "The number $y(t)$ of people who have participated in a viral trend on social media follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=1250y-5{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=40,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in hours, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible number of participants?\n\nThe maximum possible number of participants is\n{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible number of participants in the trend. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/d8133f1c4203903bac606bbae61c73717e2ba2dc15a97a77f48eaaeaf4736d06.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032} & =1250y-5{y}^{2} \\\\  & =5y(250-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=250.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $250,$ and we conclude that the maximum possible number of participants is $250.$",
